    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T21:38:44Z",
    "body": "Claim released. STOPPED after two quick gate build failures.\n\nBoth posts leave the last rotary angles active at program end. The local fix reuses the upright return helper. It cancels TCPM with G49, retracts Z, returns the rotary axes to zero, then homes X/Y. Doosan also unclamps and clamps A.\n\nThe new tests are fanuc_returns_rotaries_before_program_end and doosan_returns_rotaries_before_program_end. Both failed before the fix. Both pass with G28 and G53 after the fix. upright_program_end_adds_no_rotary_return also passes.\n\nRestoring each post from upstream/main made its pin fail. Restoring the fix made it pass. Removing the new G49 blocks made both pins fail. Restoring those blocks made both pass.\n\ncargo xtask catalog --case multiaxis/indexed passed. Only the final blocks in indexed.nc changed. The unrelated project version change was removed.\n\nThe first cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main failed in the post build step. Rust reported E0463 for the solidcore crates in camcraft-kernel. The gate had seeded artifacts from another worktree. A targeted cargo clean removed those artifacts. The second attempt failed in the same build step with E0463 for boa_engine in crates/post/src/post/js.rs:16. No gate tests ran. The change does not alter Rust library code or dependencies.\n\nThe patch remains uncommitted in .claude/worktrees/issue-3540 on issue/3540-program-end-rotary-return. No branch was pushed. No PR was opened. Clippy, the heavy gate, and the example_catalog suite did not run because Step 7 requires this stop. Mutation logs are in /tmp/3540-mutation-*.txt. The gate logs remain in the worktree.\n\nThe other-post check found that Tormach retains the final tilt by the explicit decision in #1594. Mach4 also retains its final rotary pose. Haas and Sinumerik refuse tilted output. No other post was changed.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
